# Project conventions

<!--
Place this file at the project root as `CLAUDE.md` (committed) or `.claude/CLAUDE.md`.
For personal-only overrides on this project, use `CLAUDE.local.md` and gitignore it.

Aim to keep this under 200 lines. Longer files load fully but adherence drops.
When this grows past 200 lines, split into:
- .claude/rules/<topic>.md for topical guidance (optionally `paths:`-gated)
- .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md for reference material loaded on-demand
-->

## Stack

- Language: TypeScript with strict mode
- Framework: React 19 (functional components only)
- State: Zustand for client state, TanStack Query for server state
- Testing: Vitest + Testing Library
- Build: Vite
- Package manager: pnpm (do not use npm or yarn — lockfile is pnpm-lock.yaml)

## Commands

- Install: `pnpm install`
- Dev server: `pnpm dev` (port 3001)
- Build: `pnpm build`
- Test: `pnpm test` (single run) or `pnpm test:watch`
- Lint: `pnpm lint`
- Typecheck: `pnpm typecheck`
- Format: `pnpm format`

## Project structure

- `src/api/` — backend route handlers (Hono)
- `src/components/` — React components, colocated with their tests
- `src/hooks/` — custom React hooks
- `src/lib/` — pure utilities, no React imports
- `src/server/` — server-only code, do not import from client modules

## Conventions

- Named exports only, never default exports
- Tests live next to source: `foo.ts` → `foo.test.ts`
- All API routes return `{ data: T } | { error: string }` — never throw across the route boundary
- Use `import type { ... }` for type-only imports to keep the bundle clean
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow

## Workflow

- Run tests before committing
- Run typecheck and lint before opening a PR
- Commit messages follow conventional commits (feat/fix/chore/docs/refactor)
- One logical change per PR; keep PRs reviewable

## Never

- Modify files in `dist/` or `node_modules/` directly
- Commit `.env` files or anything in `secrets/`
- Use `console.log` in production code (use the `logger` from `src/lib/log.ts`)
- Disable tests to make a build pass — fix the test or the code
